r": "internal-review-repo", "execution_id": "a2ad063b743f7b7610fd1776c59c20e1", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_012PHDKYZAAq49u9zs4zi28v", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian/pr && git pull -q origin dev 2>&1 | tail -1; grep -n \"1283\\|−0.162\\|-0.162\" paper/sections/results.tex | head; grep -n \"absolute held-out\" paper/sections/results.tex | cut -c1-700; cat results/bias_reference.csv | tail -3; git l…", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/pr && git pull -q origin dev 2>&1 | tail -1; grep -n \"1283\\|−0.162\\|-0.162\" paper/sections/results.tex | head; grep -n \"absolute held-out\" paper/sections/results.tex | cut -c1-700; cat results/bias_reference.csv | tail -3; git log -1 --format=%H"]], "output": "```console\n73:The gains must be read next to absolute held-out $R^2$ of log $|{\\rm bias}|$: on the 1224 cells where the exact bias prediction exists, every data-computable predictor has a negative absolute held-out $R^2$ ($\\bar S$ $-0.22$, noise-adjusted $S$ $-0.06$, corner times curvature $-0.12$, the best degree benchmark $p(1-p)$ $-0.26$), while the exact prediction, which needs the true response, reaches 0.987. The exploratory noise-adjusted $S$ gains 0.20 [0.10, 0.30] over a degree benchmark whose own absolute $R^2$ is negative. We conclude that these data give \\emph{no evidence of a useful data-computable bias score}, which is not evidence that none exists: the intervals include both. A reading that fits the other results is that the bias is determined by the response at the corners, which data inside the observed exposure range do not identify; this is an interpretation, not a separate test. The score also does not flag a wrong feature graph: with 10\\% and 30\\% of edges missing the bias moves from 0 to $-0.057$ and $-0.162$ while $S$ falls from 0.273 to 0.217 (Appendix~\\ref{app:extra}).\n73:The gains must be read next to absolute held-out $R^2$ of log $|{\\rm bias}|$: on the 1224 cells where the exact bias prediction exists, every data-computable predictor has a negative absolute held-out $R^2$ ($\\bar S$ $-0.22$, noise-adjusted $S$ $-0.06$, corner times curvature $-0.12$, the best degree benchmark $p(1-p)$ $-0.26$), while the exact prediction, which needs the true response, reaches 0.987. The exploratory noise-adjusted $S$ gains 0.20 [0.10, 0.30] over a degree benchmark whose own absolute $R^2$ is negative. We conclude that these data give \\emph{no evidence of a useful data-computable bias score}, which is not evidence that none exists: the intervals include both. A reading t\nmean_degree,-0.26370435667859016,1224\np(1-p),-0.2567438344965258,1224\nn p(1-p)/d,-0.26327967811458186,1224\n47da74ab19b801f0b9223e2db3bb42354366200b\n\nShell cwd was reset to /hutian/repo\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "517a55a5-84a2-57a3-9bb4-d2e4e4d7be68", "at": 1795653191.3149817, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 106242, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "internal-review-repo", "actor": "internal-review-repo", "execution_id": "a2ad063b743f7b7610fd1776c59c20e1", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "c31299e3-dd32-5ef1-9d12-c569ef55a582", "at": 1795653191.4000168, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 106244, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "internal-review-repo", "actor": "internal-review-repo", "execution_id": "a2ad063b743f7b7610fd1776c59c20e1", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "dbf0b75e-9e5d-53b8-8583-b8980b3d8976", "at": 1795653191.404632, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 106245, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "se